# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository, whatever a contributor's
# local `core.autocrlf` happens to be. Measured before this file was added:
# `git ls-files --eol` reported ZERO tracked files stored CRLF, so this pins the
# behaviour the repository already has rather than changing any content.
#
# It matters because the repository takes outside pull requests: without it, a
# contributor whose git is configured differently can commit CRLF, and the diff
# arrives as every line of a file changed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary-ish assets git should not touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
